    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Read the ASCII art of a seesaw and determine whether it is in balance.<br><br>The drawing shows blocks stacked on a continuous surface. Each <const>#</const> represents an equal mass at the center of its column. Spaces have no mass. The last line contains the support, marked by <const>X</const>. The support does not contribute mass. The <const>#</const> characters in the surface do contribute mass.<br><br>Columns are numbered from <const>0</const> on the left. The horizontal <strong>center of mass</strong> is the average column number of all <const>#</const> characters. Vertical positions do not affect this value.<br><br>The support is centered on the column of <const>X</const> and is one column wide: it extends half a column to each side. The seesaw is in balance when its center of mass is inside this interval, <strong>including both edges</strong>. Do not round or truncate the center of mass.<br><br>Print <const>In balance</const> if the seesaw is in balance. Otherwise, print <const>Not in balance</const>.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer <var>N</var>, the number of lines in the drawing.<br><strong>Next <var>N</var> lines:</strong> A string <var>line</var> containing one line of the drawing. Preserve spaces.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">One line: <const>In balance</const> if the center of mass is within the support, including its edges. Otherwise, <const>Not in balance</const>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">2 &le; <var>N</var> &le; 100<br>1 &le; length of each <var>line</var> &le; 500<br>The first <var>N</var> &minus; 1 lines contain only <const>#</const> and spaces, with at least one <const>#</const> in total.<br>The last line contains exactly one <const>X</const> and otherwise only spaces.<br>The penultimate line is a continuous surface of <const>#</const> characters, optionally surrounded by spaces.<br>Every <const>#</const> above the surface has another <const>#</const> directly below it.<br>The <const>X</const> is directly below a <const>#</const> of the surface.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">4\n#\n#####            ####\n#####################\n         X</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">In balance</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
